WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.190 --> 00:00:02.528
We strive to create a space for amazing

2
00:00:02.528 --> 00:00:04.888
and courageous people to share their stories here

3
00:00:04.888 --> 00:00:08.107
at the show, and in the wake of the senseless attacks

4
00:00:08.107 --> 00:00:10.829
on the Asian community across our country,

5
00:00:10.829 --> 00:00:14.820
many business owners and influencers are using their voice

6
00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:17.288
to speak out against hate and injustice.

7
00:00:17.288 --> 00:00:19.639
And we always want to use this platform to

8
00:00:19.639 --> 00:00:21.800
elevate these voices.

9
00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:24.927
And so, I really want you to meet our friend, Sahra Nguyen.

10
00:00:24.927 --> 00:00:28.898
She is the founder of Nguyen Coffee Supply,

11
00:00:28.898 --> 00:00:33.257
the first specialty Vietnamese coffee importer and roaster

12
00:00:33.257 --> 00:00:37.579
in the US, and Sarah has been using her business to fight

13
00:00:37.579 --> 00:00:41.410
for racial justice, one bean at a time.

14
00:00:41.410 --> 00:00:44.122
And Sarah is here in the studio!

15
00:00:44.122 --> 00:00:46.118
(audience woots)

16
00:00:46.118 --> 00:00:47.840
Hi, Drew!

17
00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:49.720
First of all, you went to UCLA

18
00:00:49.720 --> 00:00:53.172
and studied Asian American studies.

19
00:00:53.172 --> 00:00:56.520
What made it so important

20
00:00:56.520 --> 00:01:00.010
for you to have other people's back

21
00:01:00.010 --> 00:01:01.950
and fight for what you believe in?

22
00:01:01.950 --> 00:01:03.830
Yeah, I think, you know, growing up in Boston,

23
00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:07.192
I just felt so invisible as a young Vietnamese American kid.

24
00:01:07.192 --> 00:01:10.530
And then when I discovered activism in high school, I just

25
00:01:10.530 --> 00:01:12.257
I found my voice, and I found my passion

26
00:01:12.257 --> 00:01:13.950
for increasing representation

27
00:01:13.950 --> 00:01:15.430
because I didn't have that growing up.

28
00:01:15.430 --> 00:01:17.860
See, these are why I love hearing this

29
00:01:17.860 --> 00:01:20.641
because people it's like, that's your truth

30
00:01:20.641 --> 00:01:23.117
of who you are as a human being.

31
00:01:23.117 --> 00:01:25.560
And it's such an inspiration to other people.

32
00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:28.481
Now here's a fun fact, Vietnam

33
00:01:28.481 --> 00:01:33.481
number two behind Brazil for coffee production.

34
00:01:33.910 --> 00:01:36.300
Yes, I don't know until 2016.

35
00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:37.133
And I was like

36
00:01:37.133 --> 00:01:39.433
"how do I not know this fact? I'm Vietnamese American."

37
00:01:39.433 --> 00:01:42.230
Drew, it's because of lack of transparency,

38
00:01:42.230 --> 00:01:44.500
and because Vietnamese coffee and farmers have

39
00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:46.870
been rendered invisible in the coffee world.

40
00:01:46.870 --> 00:01:48.380
Well, let's bring this into the light.

41
00:01:48.380 --> 00:01:50.610
Take me through this beautiful coffee of yours.

42
00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:53.070
Yeah, so I brewed you a phin drip coffee.

43
00:01:53.070 --> 00:01:54.210
You flip the cap.

44
00:01:54.210 --> 00:01:57.020
Yep, the cap becomes a coaster, put it over.

45
00:01:57.020 --> 00:01:58.420
And I already put a dab

46
00:01:58.420 --> 00:01:59.778
of sweetened condensed milk for you in the bottle.

47
00:01:59.778 --> 00:02:01.530
You can stir it up.

48
00:02:01.530 --> 00:02:02.440
And this is Loyalty.

49
00:02:02.440 --> 00:02:03.760
It's our best-selling blend.

50
00:02:03.760 --> 00:02:05.180
And it's a blend of both Arabica

51
00:02:05.180 --> 00:02:08.454
and Robusta, which Vietnam is the most famous for.

52
00:02:08.454 --> 00:02:11.043
Thank you for letting us shine a light

53
00:02:11.043 --> 00:02:12.580
on your small business,

54
00:02:12.580 --> 00:02:14.970
which is really a big thing at this show.

55
00:02:14.970 --> 00:02:16.012
I learned so much

56
00:02:16.012 --> 00:02:19.593
about how important it is to feature small businesses.

57
00:02:23.860 --> 00:02:24.693
Whoa!

58
00:02:26.050 --> 00:02:27.650
So, it's a little stronger than usual

59
00:02:27.650 --> 00:02:29.690
because Robusta has two times more caffeine

60
00:02:29.690 --> 00:02:30.930
than Arabica coffee beans.

61
00:02:30.930 --> 00:02:32.860
There's a really delicious note

62
00:02:32.860 --> 00:02:34.998
of like a beautiful bitterness

63
00:02:34.998 --> 00:02:37.900
that's almost like a dark chocolate

64
00:02:37.900 --> 00:02:39.910
and then I'm just getting velvet.

65
00:02:39.910 --> 00:02:42.680
It's so smooth and so beautiful.

66
00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:46.270
Now, how can the rest of us really be an ally

67
00:02:46.270 --> 00:02:49.650
in this time where we want to support each other?

68
00:02:49.650 --> 00:02:51.520
Do you have a suggestion for me

69
00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:53.170
or anyone who may be watching?

70
00:02:53.170 --> 00:02:54.620
First, check in with yourself,

71
00:02:54.620 --> 00:02:56.899
and see if you have certain biases or stereotypes

72
00:02:56.899 --> 00:03:00.010
about Asians that you don't understand, so unpack that first

73
00:03:00.010 --> 00:03:01.630
because change starts inside.

74
00:03:01.630 --> 00:03:03.620
And then the next thing, is to use your voice

75
00:03:03.620 --> 00:03:05.184
and your platform and your privilege to have

76
00:03:05.184 --> 00:03:07.410
these conversations with other people.

77
00:03:07.410 --> 00:03:08.780
Because when we can start one-on-one,

78
00:03:08.780 --> 00:03:10.185
it creates a ripple effect with change.

79
00:03:10.185 --> 00:03:11.823
I also reached out to all

80
00:03:11.823 --> 00:03:15.886
of my friends and I just said, "What can I do?

81
00:03:15.886 --> 00:03:18.400
How can I be there for you?"

82
00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:20.060
I love what you just shared because it shows

83
00:03:20.060 --> 00:03:22.820
that being an ally and being a change-maker,

84
00:03:22.820 --> 00:03:24.910
it's not a perfect path and it's not a linear path.

85
00:03:24.910 --> 00:03:27.788
It's about being open to learning and stumbling and growing.

86
00:03:27.788 --> 00:03:30.520
I think that's just the most important thing, right?

87
00:03:30.520 --> 00:03:31.891
And so, thank you for reaching out.

88
00:03:31.891 --> 00:03:32.990
You're being so honest

89
00:03:32.990 --> 00:03:35.340
and vulnerable about your experience, as well.

90
00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:36.619
Thank you, Sahra!

91
00:03:36.619 --> 00:03:38.450
And, are we now best friends?

92
00:03:38.450 --> 00:03:39.293
Yes, I hope so! Please!

93
00:03:39.293 --> 00:03:41.748
Oh my God! Well, we want to continue supporting

94
00:03:41.748 --> 00:03:43.540
all the good work you're doing,

95
00:03:43.540 --> 00:03:46.729
which is why we're also going to buy a $5,000 cup of coffee

96
00:03:46.729 --> 00:03:50.859
from your store, and we're gonna put you on the website,

97
00:03:50.859 --> 00:03:52.320
the whole business.

98
00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:55.720
And you are, I'm so honored

99
00:03:55.720 --> 00:04:00.030
if you will be in our small businesses gift guide.

100
00:04:00.030 --> 00:04:02.290
Are you kidding? Woo! Ah!

101
00:04:02.290 --> 00:04:03.360
And, thank you, Sahra.

102
00:04:03.360 --> 00:04:06.527
(upbeat music begins)

